BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45 209.89 Td (Current emergency management workflows suffer from four fatal architectural flaws:) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 47 192.39 Td (1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 192.39 Td (Unverified & Stale Geolocation: Civilians struggle to communicate precise street addresses under) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 178.89 Td (panic, while laptop and desktop browsers frequently suffer from Wi-Fi MAC BSSID cache errors,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 165.39 Td (returning coordinates displaced thousands of kilometers away from the real incident.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 47 149.89 Td (2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 149.89 Td (Disconnected First Responders: Responders lack a dedicated mobile-friendly tactical interface to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 136.39 Td (acknowledge dispatches, log timestamped progress \(En Route, On Scene\), and communicate mission) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 122.88999999999999 Td (completion back to central command.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 47 107.38999999999999 Td (3.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 107.38999999999999 Td (Resource Starvation & Negative Stocking: Physical resources \(ICU beds, trauma kits, search vehicles\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 93.88999999999999 Td (are allocated ad-hoc without transactional row locking, leading to race conditions, inventory) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 80.38999999999999 Td (overselling, and orphaned allocations when missions end.) Tj ET
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 47 64.88999999999999 Td (4.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 61 64.88999999999999 Td (Information Asymmetry in Hospitals: Healthcare facilities operate isolated inventory spreadsheets,) Tj ET
